Rule 1 (grayscale input: last dimension size must be 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1
>>
Rule 2 (images dtype must be numeric: disallow bool/complex/str/dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 3 (images must be a TensorFlow tensor to avoid AttributeError about get_shape)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (non-channel dimensions are positive when rank ≥ 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 2] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
